  <header class="masthead">
    <div class="kicker">Lost Science of Prophetic Engineering · Chart&nbsp;VI·d · Plate&nbsp;30</div>
    <h1>Chronotecture
      <span class="sub">622&nbsp;AD [4516&nbsp;AM] — six spans, each run twice</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="prov">A rebuild of Jason&nbsp;M.&nbsp;Breshears’ hand-drawn chart&nbsp;VI·d (Breshears&nbsp;’07), with every date, span and annotation preserved verbatim; only the visual language is new. Its structural key: <b>622&nbsp;AD [4516&nbsp;AM], the Islamic Hijrah Calendar</b>. Each bar runs a span from 622&nbsp;AD to a medieval event, then <b>the same span again</b> to a later one: 622, 632, 692, 711, 726 and 734 years. The ruler is marked in 50-year jubilees and ends at 6000&nbsp;AM [2106&nbsp;AD]. “Principle icon of a black meteoric rock in Kaaba.”</p>
  </header>

